Short:        Simple, macOS-inspired Workbench dock
Author:       renewable-intel
Uploader:     renew.intel.soft@gmail.com (renewable-intel)
Type:         util/wb
Version:      1.0
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.2.0
Requires:     AmigaOS 3.2, 68030+ with fast RAM
URL:          https://github.com/renewable-intel/SimpleDock

SimpleDock is an app dock at the edge of your Workbench screen, in the
style of the macOS dock.

  - click to start, drag to rearrange, drag off to remove
  - drop Workbench icons between dock icons to add them, onto an icon
    to open them with it
  - labels below the icons, on hover (with a small pointer, like
    macOS), or labels only
  - six colours or your own (colour picker), solid or transparent
  - auto-hide with a smooth slide, a hotkey to bring the dock out,
    optionally always in front of other windows
  - a settings window with simple and advanced settings (Dock menu in
    the Workbench menu bar); everything in one plain text file, the same
    keywords as tooltypes
  - ARexx port SIMPLEDOCK: show/hide, add/remove/move icons, change and
    save any setting from scripts
  - optional crash reports, to send with a bug report

Minimum: AmigaOS 3.2, a 68030 with fast RAM.
Recommended: a 68040/68060 accelerator or a PiStorm / Emu68 system, and
a graphics card (Picasso96) with a 16- or 24-bit screen mode.

Nothing to install: put the drawer anywhere and double-click SimpleDock.
Full documentation in the ReadMe.

Free software, GNU GPL version 3 or later. Source code:
https://github.com/renewable-intel/SimpleDock (tag v1.0)
